  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved employment outcomes for youth, women, and crisis-afflicted populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support integrated measures for just transitions and foster greater coherence in multilateral initiatives. This will be done through leveraging synergies with work under different outcomes and mainstreamed approaches. 
The ILO will facilitate knowledge development and formulate policy recommendations on the effective implementation of labour and social security laws on domestic work. Lastly, the ILO will improve the coherence and effectiveness of its approach to crisis response, peace, and resilience and ensure the implementation of constituent-led interventions at all stages of the Humanitarian-Development-Peace-Nexus (HDPN), with a focus on people made particularly vulnerable by crises, including those that are forcibly displaced. 
From a Gender and nondiscriminatory approach, this Result will increase evidence-based knowledge products, facilitate knowledge exchange, and build Arab narratives and approaches for strengthening the care economy that would pave the way for countries in the Arab States to start taking concrete measures to realize sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
